                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>John Gisbourne married <persName key="REV01">Maria Reveley</persName> in
                            May 1800. According to her <title>DNB</title> entry, he dies 1835/6.</p>
                        <p>There must some doubt over the identification of the early entries as
                            there are references to Gisborne in the diary before he marries Reveley
                            (one each year in 1795, 1797, 1798, and 1799). There is also a reference
                            to Mrs Gisborne's on 4 July 1797 . The 1799 reference is to Gisbourne
                            and MR, but the two previous entries are to Gisbournes. It is possible
                            this refers to Gisborne and a brother, but it is Godwin's usual way of
                            referring to husbands and wives; which suggests that the three early
                            references are to another Gisborne. These early entries are, however,
                            the only ones in doubt.</p>
                        <p>There is no reference in the biographies to Godwin knowing Gisborne
                            before he secretively married Maria, but there is no reason why Godwin
                            might not have known him.</p>
                        <p>Ed Pope adds: The first entry may not be
                            John Gisborne e.g. Thomas G MD Clifford St London 1785, 1790, doctor to
                            George III, died 1806.(Dairy ammended accordingly)</p><p> From 1796 the Reveleys' next-door neighbour in
                            Lisson Street was Esther Gisborne, mother of Mrs Reveley's future
                            husband; she set up a school there with the help of her daughters, three
                            of whom later married men of some renown (Muzio Clementi, Anthony
                            Vandyke Copley Fielding and John Varley). Godwin and Wollstonecraft (by
                            then Mrs Godwin) took tea there after dining at Mrs Reveley's on 4th
                            July 1797 and some Gisbornes turned up again when Godwin dined at
                            Reveley's on 15th August 1798. Godwin bumped into John Gisborne and Mrs
                            Reveley together on 3rd December 1799, five months before their marriage
                            and five months after her husband's death. The Gisbornes went to live in
                            Italy where they later met Godwin's daughter Mary Shelley. (see my
                            Blog/Article "William Godwin, the Reveleys and the Jenningses" from
                            which this paragraph is mostly pasted, and note [16] Winchelsea House,
                            Lisson St ladies boarding school, Mrs G widow of wine merchant of Cannon
                            St PCC 1786 Zachariah G of Upper Clapton wine merchant, father in law
                            John Rogers, wife Esther, sister Sarah wife of Roger hall of Walsall
                            butcher dated 12.8.1786. He married Esther Rogers at St Benet Pauls
                            Wharf 27.9.1772. John was their eldest child born 6.9.1773 bapt St Mary
                            at Hill 30.9.1773; then Sarah born 12.12.1774 bapt there 5.1.1775; Anna
                            Maria born 25.2.1776 bapt St Martin Ongar and St Clement Eastcheap
                            17.3.1776 (bur 23.1.1820 St Mary Whitechapel age 43); Zachariah born
                            10.7.1777 bapt 6.8.1777 there; Esther born 21.12.1779 and bapt 19.1.1780
                            St Mary Abchurch (=John Varley); Thomas bapt Hackney St John 22.12.1781;
                            Susannah bapt there 9.7.1783 (= AVCFielding); Emma bapt there 29.1.1785
                            (=Muzio Clementi). Lived at the Grove, Highgate. John G will PCC 1836
                            Plymouth, Maria G dau of John James decd, Elizabeth Rumble servant, exec
                            Wm Curtis bookseller Wimpole St. Maria G nee James died 27.4.1836
                            Windsor Pl, Plymouth. Esther G will PCC 1841 Brighton</p>
                    </note>
